        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (91.2 mg, 0.2 mmol) and Schiff base ligand H3L (0.0358 g, 0.1 mmol) were reacted in 1:1 methanol/acetonitrile in the presence of sodium hydroxide. The solution was stirred for 5 h at room temperature and filtered. The filtrate was left undisturbed for slow solvent evaporation, giving yellow single crystals after a week.",
